cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
title: "Lid-Driven Cavity with a Corrugated Floor: Mechanical Energy Budget"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-16"
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/Ahmedalgeria778/Lid_driven_ondulation/blob/main/LICENSE"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ahmedalgeria778/Lid_driven_ondulation"
url: "https://github.com/Ahmedalgeria778/Lid_driven_ondulation"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation and data set for the numerical study of the steady
  incompressible flow in a two-dimensional lid-driven cavity with a sinusoidally
  corrugated bottom wall and a controlled moving-lid velocity profile. The global
  mechanical-energy budget (lid power P*, viscous dissipation D*, kinetic energy
  K*) is quantified for a family of corrugation geometries and lid profiles. The
  reference solver is a D2Q9 multiple-relaxation-time (MRT) lattice-Boltzmann
  scheme with an interpolated (Bouzidi) bounce-back treatment of the curved wall;
  an independent Taylor-Hood P2/P1 finite-element solver is used for
  cross-validation. A manuscript accompanies the code and data.
